# MCP Server Implementation for Angband Variant

## Overview
This document outlines the implementation strategy for Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers in our Angband variant, enabling AI-driven emergent gameplay through standardized communication with LLMs.

## Development Workflow

### 1. Planning Phase
- Define the specific gameplay elements that will use AI
- Map required AI capabilities to specific MCP tools
- Design the authentication and security approach
- Create specifications for each tool's parameters and outputs
- Develop error handling and fallback strategies

### 2. Implementation Phase

#### Core Server Structure
```c
/**
 * Initialize the MCP server for game integration
 */
mcp_server_t *
init_mcp_server(const char *server_name, int port)
{
    mcp_server_t *server = malloc(sizeof(mcp_server_t));
    
    if (server == NULL) {
        return NULL;
    }
    
    server->name = strdup(server_name);
    server->port = port;
    server->tools = create_tool_registry();
    server->active = false;
    
    return server;
}

/**
 * Register a tool with the MCP server
 */
bool
register_mcp_tool(mcp_server_t *server, const char *tool_name, 
                 tool_handler_t handler, tool_params_t *params)
{
    if (server == NULL || tool_name == NULL || handler == NULL) {
        return false;
    }
    
    mcp_tool_t *tool = create_tool(tool_name, handler, params);
    
    if (tool == NULL) {
        return false;
    }
    
    return add_tool_to_registry(server->tools, tool);
}
```

#### Tool Implementation Examples

##### Narrative Generation Tool
```c
/**
 * Generate narrative description based on game state
 */
char *
generate_narrative_handler(const char *location, const char *context, void *user_data)
{
    game_state_t *state = (game_state_t *)user_data;
    
    // Prepare prompt with context
    char prompt[4096];
    snprintf(prompt, sizeof(prompt), 
             "[GAME_STATE]\n%s\n[/GAME_STATE]\n"
             "[LOCATION]\n%s\n[/LOCATION]\n"
             "[CONTEXT]\n%s\n[/CONTEXT]\n"
             "[INSTRUCTION]\nGenerate a vivid, atmospheric description of this location "
             "that reflects the game state and context.\n[/INSTRUCTION]",
             serialize_game_state(state), location, context);
    
    // Request from LLM
    char *response = request_llm_completion(state->llm_client, prompt);
    
    // Process and validate response
    char *validated = validate_narrative_response(response);
    free(response);
    
    return validated;
}
```

##### Combat Analysis Tool
```c
/**
 * Analyze combat situation and suggest enemy tactics
 */
combat_response_t *
analyze_combat_handler(entity_t *player, entity_t **enemies, int enemy_count, void *user_data)
{
    game_state_t *state = (game_state_t *)user_data;
    combat_response_t *response = malloc(sizeof(combat_response_t));
    
    if (response == NULL) {
        return NULL;
    }
    
    // Prepare combat state representation
    char *combat_state = serialize_combat_state(player, enemies, enemy_count);
    
    // Prepare prompt
    char prompt[4096];
    snprintf(prompt, sizeof(prompt),
             "[COMBAT_STATE]\n%s\n[/COMBAT_STATE]\n"
             "[INSTRUCTION]\nAnalyze this combat situation and suggest appropriate "
             "tactics for the enemies based on their abilities, the environment, "
             "and the player's condition.\n[/INSTRUCTION]",
             combat_state);
    
    free(combat_state);
    
    // Request from LLM
    char *llm_response = request_llm_completion(state->llm_client, prompt);
    
    // Parse and validate response
    parse_combat_response(llm_response, response);
    free(llm_response);
    
    return response;
}
```

##### Lore Retrieval Tool
```c
/**
 * Retrieve lore information about a character, location, or artifact
 */
lore_response_t *
get_lore_handler(const char *entity_name, const char *entity_type, const char *age, void *user_data)
{
    game_state_t *state = (game_state_t *)user_data;
    lore_response_t *response = malloc(sizeof(lore_response_t));
    
    if (response == NULL) {
        return NULL;
    }
    
    // First check the memory bank cache
    lore_entry_t *cached_lore = lore_manager_get_entry(entity_name, entity_type, age);
    
    if (cached_lore != NULL) {
        // Use cached lore
        response->content = strdup(cached_lore->content);
        response->source = strdup(cached_lore->source);
        response->age = strdup(cached_lore->age);
        response->year = cached_lore->year;
        response->is_canonical = cached_lore->is_canonical;
        return response;
    }
    
    // If not in cache, prepare a request to the LLM
    char prompt[4096];
    snprintf(prompt, sizeof(prompt),
             "[ENTITY]\n%s\n[/ENTITY]\n"
             "[ENTITY_TYPE]\n%s\n[/ENTITY_TYPE]\n"
             "[AGE]\n%s\n[/AGE]\n"
             "[INSTRUCTION]\nProvide accurate lore information about this entity from "
             "Tolkien's legendarium. If the information is not canonical, indicate this "
             "clearly and provide the closest canonical reference.\n[/INSTRUCTION]",
             entity_name, entity_type, age);
    
    // Request from LLM
    char *llm_response = request_llm_completion(state->llm_client, prompt);
    
    // Parse and validate response
    parse_lore_response(llm_response, response);
    free(llm_response);
    
    // Add to cache for future use
    lore_manager_add_entry(entity_name, entity_type, age, response);
    
    return response;
}
```

##### Narrative Generation with Lore Context
```c
/**
 * Generate narrative content that incorporates lore context
 */
char *
generate_lore_narrative_handler(const char *content_type, const char *entity_name, 
                               const char *age, void *user_data)
{
    game_state_t *state = (game_state_t *)user_data;
    
    // Retrieve relevant lore first
    lore_response_t *lore = get_lore_handler(entity_name, content_type, age, user_data);
    
    if (lore == NULL) {
        return strdup("Could not retrieve lore information.");
    }
    
    // Prepare prompt with lore context
    char prompt[4096];
    snprintf(prompt, sizeof(prompt), 
             "[GAME_STATE]\n%s\n[/GAME_STATE]\n"
             "[ENTITY]\n%s\n[/ENTITY]\n"
             "[LORE_CONTEXT]\n%s\n[/LORE_CONTEXT]\n"
             "[AGE]\n%s\n[/AGE]\n"
             "[INSTRUCTION]\nGenerate %s narrative content about this entity that "
             "incorporates the lore context. Ensure the narrative is consistent with "
             "the lore and appropriate for the age. Focus on creating an immersive "
             "experience that feels authentic to Tolkien's world.\n[/INSTRUCTION]",
             serialize_game_state(state), entity_name, lore->content, age, content_type);
    
    // Request from LLM
    char *response = request_llm_completion(state->llm_client, prompt);
    
    // Process and validate response
    char *validated = validate_narrative_response(response);
    free(response);
    free_lore_response(lore);
    
    return validated;
}
```

### 3. Testing Phase
- Unit test each tool function
- Integration test with mock LLM responses
- Performance testing under various load conditions
- Edge case testing with unusual inputs
- User experience testing in gameplay context
- Lore accuracy validation with canonical sources

## Security Considerations
- Implement proper authentication for MCP server access
- Sanitize all inputs before processing
- Validate all LLM outputs before applying to game state
- Implement rate limiting to prevent abuse
- Provide fallback mechanisms for offline play
- Verify lore sources to prevent misinformation

## Performance Optimization
- Cache common responses to reduce LLM calls
- Implement asynchronous processing for non-blocking gameplay
- Batch similar requests when possible
- Use lightweight models for time-sensitive operations
- Implement progressive enhancement based on available resources
- Pre-load frequently accessed lore on startup
- Use LRU caching for lore entries 